														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4833935">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Musical</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Basic layout</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
-SCP is a sentient vintage ham radio that produces various forms of music to living things that enter its radius.<br />
-The music in-question is based off the person's history, personality, how other people view them and in the case of other SCPs or other anomalous entities, their abilities. It can also play music to what would otherwise fit the scenario in-question (if its a containment breach its going to sound out chase music mixed in with the leitmotifs of the other SCPs that are part of the breach, etc, etc.)<br />
-The SCP can teleport to a place that is having a suitably dramatic moment and play said music or otherwise to a person that it has played music to before and is 'bored.'</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Don't have a narrative per say, but it could possibly shed light on other SCP's stories and personalities through song.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I've looked at a lot of other SCPs and while there are a couple that play songs, I haven't really seen any from my digging about that basically plays a person or SCP's own personal theme song or opera in some-cases and the fact that there is a chance for a lot of interactions with other SCPs throughout the base or the researchers in-general makes me feel like there's a lot of potential for The Song of Your Life.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> No particular concerns right now.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Desperate to escape, an infinity corrals us back in.</p>
<p>Don't let them see it, for they surely won't make it easier.</p>

